#
# Declarative structural assertions for the kernel slice — the slice-resident
# test-DSL twin of the kernel-local MUST / MUST-NOT invariants formerly
# hand-written in tests/test_aboutness.py (the universal aboutness axis, #349,
# EPIC #348). Authored as gmeow: ontology data so the native Rust harness
# (crates/slicetest, #784) drives the test, not ad-hoc Python. Each assertion
# runs as a SPARQL ASK over the kernel module graph (gmeow:scopeModule).
#
# Scope note: only the invariants whose subjects are DECLARED in the kernel
# module migrate here. test_aboutness_orthogonal_to_other_axes and
# test_no_aboutness_truth_bridge assert ABSENCE over the whole merged graph
# across axes (gmeow:confidence, gmeow:hasGranularity, …) and a seed
# (gmeow:aboutnessEnacts) that are also declared/used in 10+ other slices, so
# they cannot be faithfully reduced to module scope and are RETAINED in pytest
# (see dsl/tests/MIGRATION-LEDGER.md for the per-test pytest→DSL mapping).

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/kernel/tests/> .

# --- 1. AboutnessMode class structure (MUST hold) ----------------------------
ex:saAboutnessModeClass a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
ASK {
    gmeow:AboutnessMode a owl:Class , logic:AbstractIndividualType ;
        rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "gmeow:AboutnessMode MUST be a universal logic:AbstractIndividualType owl:Class that is a subclass of logic:QualityValue — a value vocabulary of individuals, never per-mode subclasses (Principle 9, the fourth domain-free epistemic axis #349). Mirrors test_aboutness_class_structure in test_aboutness.py." .

# --- 2. hasAboutness is an AnnotationProperty ranging on AboutnessMode (MUST) -
ex:saHasAboutnessAnnotationProperty a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:hasAboutness a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
        rdfs:range gmeow:AboutnessMode .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "gmeow:hasAboutness MUST be declared an owl:AnnotationProperty (not an ObjectProperty, unlike the other three axes) with rdfs:range gmeow:AboutnessMode — the annotation form keeps the OWL downcast DL-clean through the accordingTo pattern (Principle 3). Mirrors the positive clauses of test_has_aboutness_property_structure." .

# --- 3. hasAboutness is domain-free, non-object, non-functional (MUST-NOT) ----
ex:saHasAboutnessNotObjectFunctionalOrDomained a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    { gmeow:hasAboutness a owl:ObjectProperty . }
    UNION
    { gmeow:hasAboutness a owl:FunctionalProperty . }
    UNION
    { gmeow:hasAboutness rdfs:domain ?d . }
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The kernel declaration of gmeow:hasAboutness MUST NOT make it an owl:ObjectProperty (it is an annotation), MUST NOT make it owl:FunctionalProperty (multi-vantage classifications coexist, Principle 9), and MUST NOT give it an rdfs:domain (domain-free/universal, like hasGranularity/hasDeterminacy/hasSensitivity). Mirrors the negative clauses of test_has_aboutness_property_structure." .

# --- 4. The value vocabulary's two seeds are typed AboutnessMode (MUST) -------
ex:saAboutnessSeedsTyped a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    gmeow:aboutnessDescribes a gmeow:AboutnessMode .
    gmeow:aboutnessEnacts    a gmeow:AboutnessMode .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The mention/use space MUST be spanned by both seeds: gmeow:aboutnessDescribes (mention) and gmeow:aboutnessEnacts (use) are each a gmeow:AboutnessMode. Mirrors the membership half of test_value_vocab_spans_two_seeds." .

# --- 5. No third AboutnessMode member in the kernel module (MUST-NOT) ---------
ex:saAboutnessNoThirdMember a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    ?m a gmeow:AboutnessMode .
    FILTER (?m != gmeow:aboutnessDescribes && ?m != gmeow:aboutnessEnacts)
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The aboutness value vocabulary is a genuinely-closed two-member enumeration with no privileged winner (Principle 9): the kernel module MUST NOT declare any gmeow:AboutnessMode individual other than the describes/enacts seeds. Mirrors the closure half of test_value_vocab_spans_two_seeds (kernel-scoped; the cross-module guarantee that no OTHER slice adds a member is borne by the retained merged-graph pytest)." .
